    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Desalination is an inherently energy-intensive process. However, energy is all around us; from the hydrogen bonds formed by water to the rays of light coming from the sun. Drawing inspiration from nature, the goal of this research is to develop a new technology that harness energy from primary sources to separate brine into its two fundamental components: water and salt. Through advancements in material science and a growing understanding of the physics behind evaporation, our lab is developing an sustainable solution to off-grid desalination.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Finnerty, C., Nelson, K. L., Sedlak, D. L., & Mi, B. X. (2018). E2.18 Finnerty 2018 ReNUWIt Annual Meeting Poster. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/zz392vx8589",
